<title>UK: Swiss Bank issues securities tied to Hang Seng.</title>
<headline>Swiss Bank issues securities tied to Hang Seng.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss Bank Corp said on Tuesday it had issued 100,000 &quot;performance linked to equity&quot; securiries (Perles) tied Hong Kong's blue chip Hang Seng index.</p>
<p>The investment bank said the securities, would be issued at HK$14,065 -- 96 percent of their spot price -- and would be redeemable at the closing price of the Hang Seng on December 8, 9 and 10, 1998.</p>
<p>The securities may in future be listed on the Luxembourg stock exchange, SBC said.</p>
<p>Earlier the Hang Seng closed 215.42 points lower at 14,439.71.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 17 1542 4367</p>
</text>
